      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I agree, I really miss voice prioritization, and think the experience is much worse because it is missing. As I have to constantly turn of peoples voice across the room, because them having fun over there, is overpowering the conversation I'm having over here across the room. Who asked to have Voice Prioritization removed?? I've only heard people saying how they miss it, or how that they didn't know it was a thing. NO ONE said it was in the way or somehow diminishing the experience. \n\nMany were using it, VRC's new audio system suck because the user don't have ANY control of it. Please give us some control back!!! I want to hear what my friends are saying.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-08-05T16:27:28.389Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The new system is terrible! \n\nIt used to be that even with extremely large groups of friends, I could hear the people I was standing closest to clearly. \n\nNow, with only 7 or so people standing nearby yapping away I can hardly have a conversation with someone right in front of me unless we move a good ways away from the group... and even then they're still pretty loud unless we move far enough away that we've essentially split off into our own group, which is no good if we're there to socialize. We can't be walking 15 feet away from everyone every time we want to talk at a normal volume and not have to yell everything.\n\nThe old system was hardly perfect, because the range needed to be tweaked a bit and it would cut people out entirely if they were too far away, but this is soooo much worse! At least with the old system when it became a problem we could temporarily disable it and have what we have now, but now we're stuck with this cacophony all the time!",
